From: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott@hotmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: bridge: export br_fdb_find_rcu

Export br_fdb_find_rcu() so netfilter flow offload can check whether a
destination MAC is known in the bridge FDB when resolving a bridged flow
to a DIRECT route. Prerequisite for the nft_flow_offload bridging support
(675-02). Slim rebase of the original 675-01 for kernel 6.18.41: only the
br_fdb_find_rcu export is needed; the __dev_fill_forward_path ctx-split
refactor is dropped (675-02 uses dev_fill_forward_path instead).

---
--- a/net/bridge/br_fdb.c	2026-08-02 22:04:19.583966601 +1000
+++ b/net/bridge/br_fdb.c	2026-08-02 22:04:19.584966635 +1000
@@ -266,6 +266,7 @@
 {
 	return fdb_find_rcu(&br->fdb_hash_tbl, addr, vid);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(br_fdb_find_rcu);
 
 /* When a static FDB entry is added, the mac address from the entry is
  * added to the bridge private HW address list and all required ports
